# Everything the BuildKit context does not need. Finding 17: without this file
# `COPY . .` uploaded the 25 MB committed darwin/arm64 `server` binary into the
# build stage of every release, for both architectures.
#
# Patterns are matched against context-root-relative paths (Go filepath.Match
# semantics, not gitignore semantics), so a bare name only matches at the root.
# The build genuinely needs go.mod, go.sum, cmd/, internal/, templates/ (input
# to `templ generate`) and static/ (served from disk at runtime) — none of them
# may be listed here.

# Git metadata and CI definitions.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Host build outputs. `go build ./cmd/server` produces `server` and
# `make build` produces `kontrolplane-feed`; both are host-native binaries that
# would only bloat the context and shadow nothing useful.
server
kontrolplane-feed

# air scratch directory and local SQLite databases.
tmp
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm

# Local configuration that must never be baked into an image.
.env
.env.*

# Tooling that only applies to a developer checkout.
.air.toml
docker-compose.yaml
docker-compose.*.yaml
Makefile
.dockerignore

# Documentation and screenshots.
assets
README.md
LICENSE

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp
